# Windsurf Rules — Photo Selector Toolbox

## 1. Repository Architecture & The Five Products
This repository ships **five independent products** sharing photographic concepts (EXIF contract, score semantics, Selection folder convention) and nothing else:

| Product | Code Path | Tech Stack | Target Platform | Test Command |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Desktop** | `products/desktop` | Python 3.11+, Tkinter, Poetry, Pytest | macOS, Linux, Windows workstations | `poetry run pytest products/desktop/tests/unit -m "not visual"` |
| **Native macOS Desktop** | `products/macos-desktop` | Swift 6, SwiftUI, Apple Vision, Apple Accelerate, ImageIO | macOS 14+ / macOS 15+ Apple Silicon & Intel workstations | `swift test --package-path products/macos-desktop` |
| **Android Desktop (:android-desktop)** | `products/android/android-desktop` | Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Room, OpenCV, Vico | Samsung DeX, Android tablets >= 840 dp, Chromebooks | `./gradlew :products:android:android-desktop:testDebugUnitTest` |
| **PhotoTok (:phototok)** | `products/android/phototok` | Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, DataStore, SAF | Android phones < 600 dp, portrait, gesture-first navigation | `./gradlew :products:android:phototok:testDebugUnitTest` |
| **Shared Android Core (:core)** | `products/android/core` | Kotlin, EXIF data model & reader interfaces | Shared between :android-desktop and :phototok | `./gradlew :products:android:core:testDebugUnitTest` |
| **Linux Desktop** | `products/linux-desktop` | Python 3.11+, PyGObject, GTK4, Libadwaita, GExiv2 / PIL | Debian 13 (Trixie), GNOME 46+ workstations | `pytest products/linux-desktop/tests/` |

## 2. Non-Negotiable Invariants
- **Strict Product Isolation**: Never import or copy code between products. `products/android/core/` is the ONLY shared code between Android products.
- **Mandatory Task Lifecycle**: Always start with `ai/skills/task-lifecycle/SKILL.md` (read product REQUIREMENTS.md and ai/memory/ lessons) and conclude with `ai/skills/retrospective/SKILL.md`.
- **Comprehensive Verification**: Verify every change with `./scripts/run_tests.sh`. Never rely on partial test subsets.
- **Zero Code Review Standard**: Ensure all deliveries are accompanied by verifiable test results and requirement sync.
- **Clean Workspace Hygiene**: Never commit scratch files (`scratch*.py`, temporary logs, PR drafts).
- **Canonical Framework**: All configuration lives in `ai/`. Never hand-edit generated toolchain files.

